# A235498

For k in {2,3,...,9} define a sequence as follows: a(0)=0; for n>=0, a(n+1)=a(n)+1, unless a(n) ends in k, in which case a(n+1) is obtained by replacing the last digit of a(n) with the digit(s) of k^2. This is k(2).

The 67 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `0`.

Skeleton generated by `lake exe oeis-gen`; every declaration is a `sorry` placeholder.
-/

